[{"answer":"The planet on which we live is called the Earth.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/1.mp3"},{"answer":"Our planet is constantly moving around the sun,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/2.mp3"},{"answer":"and each year, the Earth travels all the way around the sun.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/3.mp3"},{"answer":"But there are many other planets that also travel around the sun.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/4.mp3"},{"answer":"Together with the sun, the planets, and various other bodies,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/5.mp3"},{"answer":"the Earth is part of our \"solar system\".","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/6.mp3"},{"answer":"The planet that is closest to the sun is Mercury.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/7.mp3"},{"answer":"Mercury is extremely hot, and it is much smaller than the Earth.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/8.mp3"},{"answer":"The second planet from the sun is Venus.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/9.mp3"},{"answer":"Venus is about the same size as the Earth.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/10.mp3"},{"answer":"Venus is also very hot.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/11.mp3"},{"answer":"The Earth is the third planet from the sun.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/12.mp3"},{"answer":"The Earth is unusual among the planets, because it has such a large moon.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/13.mp3"},{"answer":"The Earth is bigger than the moon, but the moon is still quite large.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/14.mp3"},{"answer":"It takes about one month for the moon to travel around the Earth.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/15.mp3"},{"answer":"The fourth planet from the sun is Mars.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/16.mp3"},{"answer":"Mars is known for its red color.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/17.mp3"},{"answer":"Mars is smaller and colder than the Earth.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/18.mp3"},{"answer":"Mars has two very small moons.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/19.mp3"},{"answer":"After the planet Mars, there are many small bodies called the asteroids.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/20.mp3"},{"answer":"These rocky objects are much smaller than the planets.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/21.mp3"},{"answer":"The first four planets are all made of rock and metal.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/22.mp3"},{"answer":"The remaining planets, however, are mostly made of frozen gases.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/23.mp3"},{"answer":"The fifth planet is called Jupiter.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/24.mp3"},{"answer":"Jupiter is the largest planet.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/25.mp3"},{"answer":"It has many moons that travel around it,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/26.mp3"},{"answer":"and it also has a large red spot.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/27.mp3"},{"answer":"The sixth planet is called Saturn.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/28.mp3"},{"answer":"Saturn is the second-largest planet, and it is famous for the wide \"rings\" that surround it.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/29.mp3"},{"answer":"These rings are made up of many smaller objects that are found in the same area.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/30.mp3"},{"answer":"The seventh planet is called Uranus.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/31.mp3"},{"answer":"The eighth planet is called Neptune.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/32.mp3"},{"answer":"These planets are also gas giants, but they are smaller than Jupiter and Saturn.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/33.mp3"},{"answer":"Both Uranus and Neptune are so far from the sun","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/34.mp3"},{"answer":"that scientists only discovered these planets during the past few hundred years, using telescopes.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/35.mp3"},{"answer":"The other planets had all been visible to curious people for many thousands of years.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/36.mp3"},{"answer":"The ninth planet is called Pluto.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/37.mp3"},{"answer":"Pluto is very small, and it is much more rocky than the gas giants.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/38.mp3"},{"answer":"Some scientists believe that Pluto is not really a planet at all.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/39.mp3"},{"answer":"They suggest that Pluto is the largest of many asteroids that are found at the edge of the solar system.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/40.mp3"},{"answer":"The solar system is a vast place.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/41.mp3"},{"answer":"So far, people have not travelled beyond the moon.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/42.mp3"},{"answer":"But perhaps someday, human astronauts will visit the other planets of our solar system!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/145-the-planets-of-our-solar-system-2019-04-07-04-29-14/43.mp3"}]
